      "id": "writeto-error-before-reset",
      "text": "Start with unread data and call WriteTo. It submits the entire unread slice in one Write call. For an in-range count, it advances by that count before checking the error. A partial count with an error returns the same error value and leaves the suffix unread. A partial count with nil error returns io.ErrShortWrite and leaves the same suffix. A full count with nil error resets immediately. A full count with an error leaves Len() at zero but leaves the consumed bytes counted against Available(). A subsequent WriteTo on that empty buffer skips the writer, resets, and returns (0, nil). A writer count above the submitted length panics before the offset changes.",
