      "id": "negative-peek-and-next",
      "text": "Start with 'xy' and successfully ReadByte once. In separate runs, call Peek(-1) or Next(-1) and recover from the slice-bounds panic. Both calls leave Len() at 1. After Peek(-1), UnreadByte succeeds and 'x' is readable again. After Next(-1), UnreadByte returns an error because Next cleared the read record before slicing. For an oversized positive request from the same starting state, Peek returns 'y' with io.EOF and leaves it unread, while Next returns 'y' and drains the buffer.",
